POSTS = [
    ('Caring for oiled wood', '<p>Wipe spills within the hour, use a damp cloth for the rest, and re-oil once a year: a thin coat, ten minutes, wipe off the excess. Scratches sand out with fine paper, then oil again.</p><p>Never varnish. Oil can be renewed for fifty years. Varnish has to be stripped.</p>', 'A hand rubbing oil into an oak table top with a cloth, in a sunlit workshop.'),
    ('Why linen wrinkles', '<p>Linen fibres are long and stiff, so they crease and they last. Stonewashing softens them before you do, and every wash after that does the rest.</p><p>Tumble low, take it out damp, and never iron. The wrinkles are the point.</p>', 'Rumpled white linen sheets on a bed in soft morning light, close up.'),
    ('Room of choice, explained', '<p>Two people bring the piece into the room you name, assemble it, and take the packaging away. It costs more than a doorstep drop, and we think it is the only way to deliver furniture.</p><p>Book a slot at checkout. We call the day before.</p>', 'Two delivery people carrying a wrapped sofa through a bright doorway.'),
]
